<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seleucus II Callinicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 246–225 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Seleucus II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus</a> II Callinicus was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> from 246 to 225 BCE. His reign began with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-syrian-war">Third Syrian War</a> against Ptolemy III, and he then fought his own brother Antiochus Hierax for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> broke away in the east. After the earthquake that ruined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> around 226 BCE he was among the kings who sent help.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seleucus-ii-callinicus.jpg" alt="Seleucus II Callinicus" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Seleucus_II_Callinicus_(cropped),_Antioch_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
